## 8. Horde Spawn System (2026-05-10, level `"horde_range"`)

Runtime wave spawner — only when `LevelState.LevelId == "horde_range"`. Drops Zombie bots on a ring around the player at fixed cadence.

- `RaidSession.Tick` calls `HordeSpawnSystem.Tick` per frame
- Grace period (`GracePeriod`, default 5s) — no spawns
- After grace: batch spawn `SpawnBatchSize` zombies on ring `SpawnRingRadius ± SpawnRingJitter` within `SpawnArc` degrees
- Cap at `MaxAlive`
- HP override per spawn: `ZombieMaxHp` from config

Driver: `DevCheatsHordeSection`. Scene: `ShootingScene_Horde.unity`.

---

## 9. Ranged-Combat Test Scene (2026-05-12, level `"ranged_range"`)

Static 7-bot layout (`RangedTarget` type) across 4 distance zones — for testing ranged combat with cover usage.

Zones:
- A (z~12-13): 2 bots in open — instant aggro
- B (z~30): 2 bots behind side walls, central pillar splits lanes
- C (z~50): asymmetric — left in L-corner, right behind straight wall
- D (z~75): 1 bot behind 10m central wall, must flank

13 cover cubes authored statically. NavMesh baked on 200×200 Plane. Spawn positions deliberately offset from cube colliders.

Spawned by `RaidSession.SpawnRangedRangeTargets()`. Scene: `ShootingScene_RangedRange.unity`.

